@startuml flow-auth
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
title Every protected request: identify, then authorise (Lab 07)

actor "Phone / curl" as C
participant "Controller" as H
participant "AuthService.identify" as A
database "users" as U
participant "authz rule" as Z
participant "Service" as S

C -> H : request + Authorization: Bearer <uid.ver.exp.sig>
H -> A : identify(header)
alt no header / bad signature / edited id
  A --> C : 401 UNAUTHORIZED
else expired
  A --> C : 401 TOKEN_EXPIRED
else signature ok
  A -> U : SELECT role, disabled, token_version WHERE id = uid
  alt disabled
    A --> C : 403 ACCOUNT_DISABLED
  else token_version differs (logout / disabled before)
    A --> C : 401 TOKEN_REVOKED
  else ok
    A --> H : Caller(id, email, role)
    H -> Z : require_admin / require_self_or_admin
    alt not allowed
      Z --> C : 403 FORBIDDEN (nothing read or changed)
    else allowed
      H -> S : operation(caller.id, ...)
      S --> C : 200 / 409 / 404 ...
    end
  end
end
note over C, S
  The phone hiding a button changes nothing here:
  the same checks run for every request.
end note
@enduml
